To hilite grouping nodes it is necessary to acquire the grouped nodes' instance keys. Adding InstanceKeysSelectQuery to the node key allows it.
• Move InstanceKeysSelectQuery from node to node key;
• Move presentation query and bound query value definitions to PublicAPI;
• Add presentation query and bound query value serialization to ECSerializer;

This does not fix label grouping nodes, another issue has been created for that. (https://github.com/iTwin/itwinjs-backlog/issues/553)

This moves creation of Web constructors and prototypes to individual "create" template specializations, then uses those to lazily create the objects the first time they are needed by way of `JS::Object::define_intrinsic_accessor`. In a profile, this drops time spent in `add_window_exposed_interfaces` just creating Window objects in an OOPWV from 14% to 0.35%.

![Screenshot from 2023-01-10 07-39-22](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/5600524/211555430-20bad788-7df0-4842-9fdc-23ce44b41bb4.png)

Example of the generated specializations, with and without a Legacy constructor:
```c++
template<>
void Intrinsics::create_web_prototype_and_constructor<HTMLOptionElementPrototype>(JS::Realm& realm)
{
    auto& vm = realm.vm();

    auto prototype = heap().allocate<HTMLOptionElementPrototype>(realm, realm);
    m_prototypes.set("HTMLOptionElement"sv, prototype);

    auto constructor = heap().allocate<HTMLOptionElementConstructor>(realm, realm);
    m_constructors.set("HTMLOptionElement"sv, constructor);

    prototype->define_direct_property(vm.names.constructor, constructor.ptr(), JS::Attribute::Writable | JS::Attribute::Configurable);
    constructor->define_direct_property(vm.names.name, JS::PrimitiveString::create(vm, "HTMLOptionElement"sv), JS::Attribute::Configurable);

    auto legacy_constructor = heap().allocate<OptionConstructor>(realm, realm);
    m_constructors.set("Option"sv, legacy_constructor);

    legacy_constructor->define_direct_property(vm.names.name, JS::PrimitiveString::create(vm, "Option"sv), JS::Attribute::Configurable);
}

template<>
void Intrinsics::create_web_prototype_and_constructor<WindowPrototype>(JS::Realm& realm)
{
    auto& vm = realm.vm();

    auto prototype = heap().allocate<WindowPrototype>(realm, realm);
    m_prototypes.set("Window"sv, prototype);

    auto constructor = heap().allocate<WindowConstructor>(realm, realm);
    m_constructors.set("Window"sv, constructor);

    prototype->define_direct_property(vm.names.constructor, constructor.ptr(), JS::Attribute::Writable | JS::Attribute::Configurable);
    constructor->define_direct_property(vm.names.name, JS::PrimitiveString::create(vm, "Window"sv), JS::Attribute::Configurable);
}
```

Related to #4911. Trimming down the public API surface area of OpenTracingShim.

OpenTracingShim contains several different factory methods allowing users to create Tracer shims using various combinations of `GlobalOpenTelemetry`, `OpenTelemetry`, `TracerProvider`, and `Tracer`. Simplified to just two methods, which becomes the total public API surface area of the entire module:
```
// Create using tracer provider and propagator from an OpenTelemetry instance
io.opentracing.Tracer createTracerShim(OpenTelemetry);
// Create using specific tracer provider, text map propagator, and http propagator
io.opentracing.Tracer createTracerShim(TracerProvider, TextMapPropagator textMapPropagator, TextMapPropagator httpPropagator);
```
If a user wants to use the global, just call `createTracerShim(GlobalOpenTelemetry.get())`. 

This allows the removal of `OpenTracingPropagators` and `OpenTracingPropagatorsBuilder`, which was just a wrapper for a TextMapPropagator and http TextMapPropagator. 

